  "id": "INV-22",
  "question": "For the Hawaii ERS 2017 PE RFP notice and 2022 PE RFP, SBCERS 2020 PE RFP, TRS Illinois FY25 PE RFP, Baltimore BCERS alternatives RFP, and Missouri LAGERS private-markets RFP, what minimum experience is required of the primary/lead consultant or, for SBCERS, at least one key professional assigned to the account?",
  "type": "broad",
  "pair_id": "",
  "status": "completed",
  "started_at_utc": "2026-10-27T09:15:31.942489+00:00",
  "available_documents": 78,
  "source_hints": null,
  "history": null,
  "answer": "| RFP | Minimum experience for the assigned consultant |\n|---|---|\n| **Hawaii ERS, 2017 PE notice** | Primary consultant: **7 years** providing domestic and international investment consulting and management services to public pension plans. (Notice, p. 1) |\n| **Hawaii ERS, 2022 PE RFP** | Primary consultant: **7 years** providing domestic and international *private equity/debt* consulting services to public pension plans. (RFP, p. 17) |\n| **SBCERS, 2020 PE RFP** | At least one key professional assigned to the account must have **10 years** recommending private-equity investments for institutional clients, including **3 years with the current firm**. The RFP separately requires at least one assigned key professional with **5 years** analyzing and monitoring institutional private-equity partnerships, and at least one with **5 years** reviewing partnership agreements and related legal documents. It does not say these must all be the same person. (RFP, p. 8) |\n| **TRS Illinois, FY25 PE RFP** | Primary consultant: **3 years** providing private-equity investment consulting to public or private pension funds, **or other highly comparable relevant experience**. (Appendix B, p. 15) |\n| **Baltimore BCERS, alternatives RFP** | Primary consultant: **5 years** consulting for public defined-benefit pension plans, plus **3 years employed by the proposing firm**. (RFP, p. 7) |\n| **Missouri LAGERS, private-markets RFP** | Lead consultant: **5 years in a lead role** recommending private-market investments across the investment verticals to U.S. public pension funds. (RFP, p. 7) |",
